Affected module: rosdistro@lyrical.2026-10-05.rcr.4 (the selected MVS release).
Failure: register_ament_files iterates every py_binary DefaultInfo output. A main
source and launcher with the same basename overwrite the installed executable;
execution reaches the original shebang and loses declared Python imports. The
registration also drops the executable's transitive runfiles.
Rationale/scope: register the FilesToRun executable for executable targets, keep
ordinary file/library registration intact, and forward input default runfiles.
Use the same selected files when applying explicit renames. No ROS source edits.
Verification: same-basename and renamed Python launchers execute with declared
imports/data; ordinary-file registration passes too (registration_test, 2 cases).
The complete wrapper, path-smoother/scenario and existing mission-launch gate
passes all eight targets with CPU/Cyclone DDS and ENABLE_AGNOCAST=0.
Upstream: published rcr.4 overlay still has both defects, checked 2026-11-22;
https://bazel.ros.org/modules/rosdistro/lyrical.2026-10-05.rcr.4/overlay/ament/ament_resource.bzl
No unpublished upstream fix association or submission is claimed.

